# Cloudflare reads this file from the build output root, same as _headers.
# Rules are matched top-to-bottom; the first match wins.

# /portfolio has never been a route on this site — the case studies live under
# /projects/. The published resume PDF and the older WordPress-era links both
# point at /portfolio, so those land on a 404 without this. 301 because the
# move is permanent and the old path has no content of its own to preserve.
/portfolio    /projects/  301
/portfolio/*  /projects/  301

# Three case studies were unpublished because their only illustration was a
# generated placeholder, which is worse than no page at all. The work was real
# but nothing survives to show, so the pages are drafts rather than deletions
# (src/content/projects, draft: true) and can come back if screenshots turn up.
# 301 to the index: the content is gone, not moved, and the index is the
# nearest useful thing.
/projects/visualize-ar/          /projects/  301
/projects/vr-simulation-toolkit/ /projects/  301
/projects/social-vr-xtraspace/   /projects/  301

# The resume was renamed when the positioning changed, and the old file is
# gone rather than left to contradict the site. A static asset would win over
# this rule, so the rename only works because the old PDF was deleted.
/Akaash-Garg-XR-Engineer-Resume.pdf  /Akaash-Garg-Systems-Architect-Resume.pdf  301
